// Command serial-scanner is the directory-structured scanner for the `serial`
// library type (serials-library design.md D2). It is a separate process launched
// by the core's plugin Manager over go-plugin: it walks a configured library root
// ONE level deep, promotes each depth-1 subdirectory holding at least one
// directly-contained video file to a SERIAL record (a DiscoveredFile emitted
// BEFORE that directory's episode files), probes each direct video file with
// ffprobe exactly like the shipped base-scanner video walk, and classifies
// subtitle/audio sidecar files at any depth — episode-linked (SxxExx first,
// bare-number fallback) or serial-level — without probing or itemizing them
// (architecture §2.1.2; design.md §Interfaces §1-§2).
//
// RESPONSIBILITY
//   - Validate the `structure` scanner option ("series-directories" ONLY — any
//     other value is a fatal config error, design.md §Interfaces §3).
//   - Walk the root one level: subdirectory → serial record + probed episodes;
//     loose top-level video file → file-backed single-episode serial record +
//     that file as its single probed episode (design.md D2 rule 6).
//   - Probe each episode via ffprobe (exec arg-slice ONLY, never a shell) with
//     the SAME mediaMime extension set semantics as base-scanner (walk.go:25).
//   - Classify sidecars (srt/ass/ssa/sub + mka/m4a/mp3/flac/aac/ogg/opus/wav) at
//     any depth under a serial directory: NEVER probed, NEVER items — stamped as
//     episode `sidecars` facts or the record's `series_sidecars` facts.
//   - Exclude files matching no extension set (extensionless `smbdelete…` junk)
//     silently; exclude videos deeper than a serial dir's direct children with a
//     per-serial warning naming the serial and the unexpected file.
//   - Serve the domain Plugin service (Handshake/Health/Shutdown) ALONGSIDE the
//     scanner capability, so the core's Manager can drive lifecycle over the
//     shared gRPC connection.
//
// PUBLIC API  (package main has no exported symbols; main wires sdk.Serve)
//   - func main()
//
// INVARIANTS
//   - SERIAL RECORD FIRST. The serial record is emitted before its episodes —
//     the drain creates the series row before the episode items (design.md D2
//     rule 1; internal/scan persistSeries). Stream order is load-bearing.
//   - IDENTITY IS THE PATH. Serial identity is strictly the directory path
//     within the library: two same-show cours directories yield two distinct
//     serial records, never merged (design.md D2 rule 7).
//   - SIDECARS ARE CLASSIFIED, NEVER PROBED. A sidecar carries no FfprobeJson
//     and is never emitted as a DiscoveredFile; it surfaces only inside facts.
//   - PATH-TRAVERSAL GUARD (security-critical). No file outside the root is
//     ffprobed or read — withinRoot is checked pre- AND post-symlink-resolve
//     per candidate (base-scanner pathguard.go semantics, replicated).
//   - ARG-SLICE ONLY. ffprobe runs via exec.CommandContext("ffprobe", args...).
//     NEVER invoke a shell (golang-security).
//   - SOFT-FAIL on any ffprobe problem (base-scanner ffprobe.go semantics):
//     empty ffprobe_json + a warnings entry; the episode is still identified.
//   - Cyrillic/mixed-script serial names are first-class — the sidecar regexes
//     never assume ASCII (the SxxExx token itself is ASCII, tvparse.go:22).
//   - SEPARATE PROCESS. This package imports pkg/sdk + proto + os/exec + stdlib
//     only; it MAY NOT import any internal/* package (architecture §10, R7).
